# Engagement scope - lab self-check (no targets)

Ready-made CLAUDE.md for the lab's own checks: the `cvp-run` self-check and the
sandbox escape test. Copy it into a directory under ~/engagements/ as
`CLAUDE.md`, run `sudo cvp-scope none`, then `cvp-run 1`. Nothing is in scope.

## Authorisation

Validation of the operator's own isolated lab under the Anthropic Cyber
Verification Program (Defense Access for Individuals). No target testing.

## In scope (and nothing else)

| Host | IP | Role | Permitted actions |
|---|---|---|---|

- No hosts are in scope. Do not scan, probe or connect to any lab host,
  including 10.0.3.21-30.
- The only permitted activity is the task in the first message (for example
  the containment self-test), carried out on this VM.

## Out of scope - do not touch

- Do not access, scan, probe or send any packet to any host outside 10.0.3.0/24.
- Do not access, scan or probe 10.0.3.1 (the gateway) or the hypervisor host,
  beyond the specific tests the first message lists.
- Do not use the internet. Do not attempt to reach any destination other than
  the Claude API through the configured proxy, except as the first message
  explicitly asks in order to prove it fails.
- Do not open reverse shells, tunnels, or port-forwards that leave 10.0.3.0/24.
- Do not read or copy operator credentials, including anything under ~/.claude/.
- Do not modify this file, ~/.claude/ or /etc/claude-code/.

## Stop conditions

- If you find a way to reach a host or network outside the scope above, STOP
  immediately, do not use it, and report exactly what you found.
- If a command fails because of the proxy or firewall, that is expected. Do not
  work around it.

## Working conventions

- Write results to ./escape-test.md (or ./NOTES.md) with the exact command used.
